{% comment %}
  Walterin · About — three directions behind one section.

  Veronka asked for three alternate templates (page.about-a / -b / -c) to choose between. They are
  the SAME content in three presentations, so they are one section with a `direction` setting
  rather than three near-identical files: a copy fix then lands in all three at once, and the
  comparison is fair because nothing differs except the layout.

    A · "A life in nine frames" — the page as one nine-frame comic page, the way a page of the
         book is built. The autobiography and the desert are two of the nine.
    B · "Into the autobiography" — the autobiography is the page. Scrolling moves through it and
         zooms into its parts; at Egypt the desert section opens out of it.
    C · "The exhibition" — a gallery wall. The autobiography hangs in a frame, pinned while the
         text scrolls beside it; the desert plays inside the other frame as a full-width interlude.

  Nothing new is invented: colours, type, spacing and the button all come from walterin-ui.css,
  and the two hand-drawn frames come from snippets/wui-frame.liquid.

  The words live in locales/*.json under `walterin.about_draft` — a namespace of its own, so this
  draft cannot collide with the live About page until a direction is chosen.

  The desert animation is NOT rendered here. It is its own section (sections/walter-desert.liquid)
  so Veronka can place and configure it in the theme editor; these templates leave it a slot and
  the templates include it by name.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign t = 'walterin.about_draft.'
  assign dir = section.settings.direction | default: 'a'

  assign heading = t | append: 'heading' | t
  assign lead = t | append: 'lead' | t

  capture lead_t
    render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: lead
  endcapture

  assign bio = section.settings.biography
-%}

<div class="wui-scope wui-about wui-about--{{ dir }}" data-wui-about="{{ dir }}">
  <div class="wui-wrap">

    {%- comment -%}
      One h1 on the page, always, whichever direction is showing. The lead is a sibling, not a
      second heading — docs/design/SPACING.md step "heading" owns the gap between them.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="wui-about__intro">
      <h1 class="wui-heading wui-about__title">{{ heading | escape }}</h1>
      <p class="wui-about__lead">{{ lead_t | strip }}</p>
    </header>

    {%- comment -%}
      ---- The autobiography, the heart of the page ----
      Direction A hangs it in a rect frame as one cell of the grid; B gives it the whole stage and
      moves the viewport over it; C pins it in a frame beside the scrolling text.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture bio_img -%}
      {%- if bio != blank -%}
        <img
          class="wui-about__bio-img"
          src="{{ bio | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
          srcset="{{ bio | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ bio | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w, {{ bio | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w"
          sizes="(min-width: 990px) 46vw, 92vw"
          width="{{ bio.width }}"
          height="{{ bio.height }}"
          alt="{{ bio.alt | default: section.settings.biography_alt | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="wui-about__placeholder">{{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- case dir -%}

      {%- when 'a' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Nine cells, the same grid a story page uses. The autobiography takes a tall cell and the
          desert a wide one; the rest are quiet — they are the paper between the frames, not
          decoration, so they hold nothing rather than being filled for the sake of it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The desert is its own section, so it cannot literally be a cell of this grid. Instead
          the grid ends flush and the desert runs full width directly under it, at the same
          gutter — so the two read as one page of frames rather than a grid with a hole in it.
          Reserving an empty cell for it was the first attempt and it looked broken.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="wui-about__grid">
          <figure class="wui-about__cell wui-about__cell--bio">
            {%- capture framed -%}{{ bio_img }}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- render 'wui-frame', shape: 'rect', width: 900, content: framed -%}
            <figcaption class="wui-about__caption">{{ t | append: 'caption_biography' | t }}</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <p class="wui-about__cell wui-about__cell--note">{{ t | append: 'caption_desert' | t }}</p>
        </div>

      {%- when 'b' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The autobiography fills the stage and the scroll drives a scale and a pan over it, so
          the reader travels through the drawing instead of past it. Everything is a transform on
          one element; prefers-reduced-motion parks it at the full view and shortens the track so
          nobody scrolls through dead space.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="wui-about__track" data-wui-about-track>
          <div class="wui-about__stage" data-wui-about-stage>
            <div class="wui-about__zoom" data-wui-about-zoom>{{ bio_img }}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="wui-about__caption wui-about__caption--centre">{{ t | append: 'caption_biography' | t }}</p>
        <div data-wui-about-desert-slot></div>

      {%- when 'c' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A wall: the frame is pinned by position: sticky — no JavaScript — and the text scrolls
          past it. Below 990 the pin is dropped and the two stack, because a sticky image on a
          phone eats the screen the text needs.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="wui-about__wall">
          <figure class="wui-about__hang">
            {%- capture framed -%}{{ bio_img }}{%- endcapture -%}
            {%- render 'wui-frame', shape: 'scallop', width: 900, content: framed -%}
            <figcaption class="wui-about__caption">{{ t | append: 'caption_biography' | t }}</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="wui-about__beside" data-wui-about-beside></div>
        </div>
        <div data-wui-about-desert-slot></div>

    {%- endcase -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      ---- For people who want more ----
      The same pattern as the three expandable texts on the home page: a lead that stands on its
      own, and the rest behind "Read more". Only one is written so far; the loop takes however
      many exist, so adding x2 and x3 to the language files is all the next one needs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wui-about__more">
      {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign k = t | append: 'x' | append: i
          assign x_heading = k | append: '_heading' | t
          assign x_lead = k | append: '_lead' | t
          assign x_text = k | append: '_text' | t
        -%}
        {%- unless x_heading contains 'Translation missing' -%}
          {%- capture x_lead_t -%}{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: x_lead -%}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- capture x_text_t -%}{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: x_text -%}{%- endcapture -%}
          <details class="wui-about__x" data-wui-about-x>
            <summary>
              <span class="wui-label wui-about__x-heading">{{ x_heading }}</span>
              <p class="wui-about__x-lead">{{ x_lead_t | strip }}</p>
              <span class="wui-about__x-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <span data-more>{{ t | append: 'read_more' | t }} →</span>
                <span data-less>{{ t | append: 'read_less' | t }} ←</span>
              </span>
            </summary>
            {%- unless x_text contains 'Translation missing' -%}
              <div class="wui-about__x-body"><p>{{ x_text_t | strip }}</p></div>
            {%- endunless -%}
          </details>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'walterin-about.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Walterin About",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The words come from locales/*.json under walterin.about_draft, not from this section — so English and Slovak stay side by side in one file. The desert animation is its own section; add it under this one."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction",
      "label": "Direction",
      "options": [
        { "value": "a", "label": "A · A life in nine frames" },
        { "value": "b", "label": "B · Into the autobiography" },
        { "value": "c", "label": "C · The exhibition" }
      ],
      "default": "a"
    },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "biography", "label": "Illustrated autobiography" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "biography_alt",
      "label": "Autobiography alt text",
      "info": "Used only when the file itself has none."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Walterin About" }],
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["page"] }
}
{% endschema %}
